<p>Ask most people to picture outdoor security lighting and they describe a motion-activated flood over the garage. It is cheap, it is bright and it is close to useless. The flood produces a cone of harsh light and a wall of blackness outside the cone. It blinds you when you step outside, washes out your security cameras, annoys the neighbors and does nothing for the side yard where someone would actually approach. Outdoor security lighting Austin homeowners should be asking for looks very different: lower, wider, warmer and always on at a modest level, so that nothing on the property is in deep shadow and nothing is glaring.</p>
